        <mxCell id="Kr28CH0wk7RwmuvBFSXC-26" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;What is blockchain for non-technical ppl?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;- &lt;/b&gt;many ppl hold identical copies, so if one changes it&#39;s obvious&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- every page is sealed to the previous one, so it has a fingerprint&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- you can&#39;t add or delete what&#39;s already there, just append&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="97" width="474" x="-215" y="-455" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Kr28CH0wk7RwmuvBFSXC-28" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why not this idea:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. Content credentials already implements this kinda&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. records sometimes require correction or permanent disposal&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. blockchain doesn&#39;t verify that something is &#39;true&#39;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4. it has been tried before -- UK National Archives ARCHANGEL project and InterPARES research group&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;5. will it still exist in 50 yrs? = long-term preservation risk&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="108" width="532" x="-241" y="-622" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
